      "stop_reason": "CANDIDATES_EXHAUSTED_FIT_SKIP",
      "text": "Ramrakhiyani et al.  proposes label propagation algorithms to discover aspects in supervisor assessments in performance appraisals, where an aspect is modelled as a verb-noun pair (e.g. conduct training, improve coding).\n\nThe\n\nSummarization of Peer Feedback using ILP\tThe PA system includes a set of peer feedback comments for each employee.\n\nEvaluation of auto-generated summaries\tWe considered a dataset of 100 employees, where for each employee multiple peer comments were recorded.\n\nThe summaries generated by our ILP-based approach were compared with the corresponding manual summaries using the ROUGE  unigram score.\n\nFor comparing performance of our ILP-based summarization algorithm, we explored a few summarization algorithms provided by the Sumy package.\n\nA common parameter which is required by all these algorithms is number of sentences keep in the final summary.\n\nILP-based summarization requires a similar parameter K, which is automatically decided based on number of total candidate phrases.\n\nThe performance of ILP-based summarization is comparable with the other algorithms, as the two sample t-test does not show statistically significant difference.\n\nsentence-based summaries.\n\nFinally, we proposed an ILP-based summarization technique to produce a summary of peer feedback comments for a given employee and compared it with manual summaries.",
